<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Havana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as La Habana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Havana is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, founded by the Spanish in 1515 and moved to its present site on a sheltered bay around 1519. It became the gathering port of the treasure fleets and was heavily fortified; it was the capital from 1607. The British held it in 1762–1763, and its old town and fortifications are a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/havana.jpg" alt="Havana" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RenaatPeeters · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DJI_0197_crp_wiki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
